    bib_know_why60_title:"Why 60 seconds works",
    bib_know_why60_tag:"Knowledge · Nervous system",
    bib_know_why60_body:"Your body doesn't just respond to hours – but to signals. Conscious breathing activates the parasympathetic system. That's the part of your nervous system that signals safety. 60 seconds is enough to interrupt the stress impulse.",
    bib_know_stressloop_title:"Stress is a cycle",
    bib_know_stressloop_tag:"Knowledge · Everyday life",
    bib_know_stressloop_body:"Stress often feels like 'too much in the head' – but it's a body state. When you briefly down-regulate (breathing, muscle tone, attention), your thinking automatically becomes clearer.",
    bib_know_panic_title:"Acute: What to do when overwhelmed",
    bib_know_panic_tag:"Knowledge · Emergency help",
    bib_know_panic_body:"When it gets acute, avoid prolonged breath-holding. Choose a calm, extended exhale. The goal isn't perfection, but a small 'I am safe' signal. Reflect afterwards.",
